(THG2-03: LANGUAGE.md:1260 says "A quoted field name prints in the quotes it
 is written with." The compiler quotes a field name in its printed output only
 when the name contains a space; a single-word name written IN quotes prints
 without them. All three fields below are written quoted; only the multi-word
 one comes back quoted. See Discrepancy 1.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox THG2-03.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   {'day sent': 25, depth: 2, altitude: 1}
)
A thing called stamp has
  a number called 'day sent' is 25,
  a number called 'depth' is 2,
  a number called 'altitude' is 1.

a stamp called posted.
